---
// Member Highlight — video-led editorial profile (Innovia member firm).
// Ported from the AGP design handoff (member-highlight-d-video). Standalone page chrome
// (its own header/footer) like the prototype; mega-menu JS intentionally omitted.
// Sample firm: Sonoran Vista Community Management. Demo data — template per the handoff.
import "../styles/tokens.css";
import "../styles/site.css";
import "../styles/member-highlight.css";
import "../styles/member-highlight-page.css";
---


  <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
  <section class="v-hero" id="top">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="crumb-wrap">
        <div class="mh-crumb">
          <a href="/">Innovia</a><span>/</span>
          <a href="/member-spotlights">Members</a><span>/</span>
          <span class="here">Sonoran Vista Community Management</span>
          <span class="verified">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            Verified Innovia member
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="v-dateline">
        <span class="place">
          <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 10c0 6-8 12-8 12s-8-6-8-12a8 8 0 0 1 16 0Z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>
          Phoenix, Arizona
        </span>
        <span class="sep"></span>
        <span>33.4484° N · 112.0740° W</span>
        <span class="sep"></span>
        <span>Maricopa County</span>
        <span class="sep"></span>
        <span>Member since 2018</span>
      </div>

      <div class="v-namerow">
        <h1>Sonoran Vista <em>Community Management.</em></h1>
      </div>
      <p class="region-tag">A Phoenix-built management company that treats the desert it serves like home — because it is. Hear it from the people who run it.</p>

      <!-- ===== VIDEO CENTERPIECE =====
           Swap the .poster-slot + .play markup for an <iframe> (YouTube/Vimeo)
           or a <video poster="…"> when the interview file is ready. -->
      <div class="v-stage-wrap">
        <div class="v-stage" id="videoStage" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Play member interview">
          <img class="v-poster" src="/assets/photos/interview-temp.jpg" alt="Inside Sonoran Vista — member interview" />
          <div class="play">
            <svg width="34" height="34" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div class="caption">
            <div class="av">MR</div>
            <div>
              <div class="ttl">Inside Sonoran Vista</div>
              <div class="sub">Marisol Reyes, Founder &amp; President · on staying independent</div>
            </div>
            <span class="runtime">4:12</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ STATS ============ -->
  <section class="v-substats tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="mh-stats">
        <div class="s"><span class="v">16<span class="u">yrs</span></span><span class="k">Serving the Valley</span></div>
        <div class="s"><span class="v">140<span class="u">+</span></span><span class="k">Communities managed</span></div>
        <div class="s"><span class="v">31k<span class="u">+</span></span><span class="k">Doors under management</span></div>
        <div class="s"><span class="v">4.9<span class="u">★</span></span><span class="k">Avg. board rating</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ STORY ============ -->
  <section class="v-story">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="head">
        <div class="eyebrow on-accent"><span class="rule-mini"></span>The story</div>
        <h2>Built one Phoenix community at a time.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="body">
        <div class="col">
          <p class="drop">Sonoran Vista started in 2009 with a single self-managed HOA in Arcadia and a founder who was tired of watching national roll-ups treat Valley communities like spreadsheet rows. The pitch was simple: a manager who actually lives here, answers the phone, and shows up at the annual meeting.</p>
          <p>That stubborn locality became the company's edge. While competitors chased volume across state lines, Sonoran Vista grew by referral — board president to board president — across Phoenix, Scottsdale, and the East Valley.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col">
          <p>By 2018, the firm faced the question every successful independent eventually does: sell to a national for the resources, or stay independent and fall behind on buying power. Joining Innovia made it a false choice.</p>
          <p>Today, 48 team members manage 140+ communities with co-op-negotiated vendor pricing behind every budget — and the same founder still personally onboards every new association.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pull">
          <p>"We never wanted to be the biggest. We wanted to be the one a board would <em>recommend without being asked.</em>"</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ FOUNDER ============ -->
  <section class="v-founder">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="frame">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="av has-photo" role="img" aria-label="Marisol Reyes"></div>
          <div class="nm">Marisol Reyes</div>
          <div class="rl">Founder &amp; President</div>
          <div class="creds"><span>CMCA</span><span>AMS</span><span>PCAM</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="copy">
          <div class="eyebrow on-accent"><span class="rule-mini"></span>Leadership</div>
          <h3>The person behind the firm — and the interview.</h3>
          <p>Marisol founded Sonoran Vista after a decade managing master-planned communities across Maricopa County. She holds the PCAM — the industry's highest management credential — and sits on the Arizona chapter board of CAI. Under her, the firm has never lost a community to a competitor on service.</p>
          <p>She brought the company into Innovia in 2018, and now represents the Southwest region on the co-op's vendor council. Hear her tell it in the interview above.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accred">
        <div class="accred-head">
          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow on-accent"><span class="rule-mini"></span>Accreditations &amp; standing</div>
            <h4>Credentialed at the firm, not just the desk.</h4>
          </div>
          <p>Beyond Marisol's personal designations, Sonoran Vista holds company-level accreditation and is a verified member in good standing of the Innovia cooperative.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="accred-grid">
          <div class="cred">
            <svg class="seal" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="8" r="6"/><path d="M15.477 12.89 17 22l-5-3-5 3 1.523-9.11"/></svg>
            <div class="ac">AAMC</div>
            <div class="fn">Accredited Association Management Company — CAI's highest firm designation</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cred">
            <svg class="seal" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg>
            <div class="ac">CAI</div>
            <div class="fn">Community Associations Institute member — Arizona Chapter</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cred">
            <svg class="seal" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h4"/><path d="M15 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7z"/><path d="m9 15 2 2 4-4"/></svg>
            <div class="ac">Licensed &amp; bonded</div>
            <div class="fn">Registered and bonded in the State of Arizona</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cred is-innovia">
            <svg class="seal" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M16 7a4 4 0 1 1-8 0"/><circle cx="12" cy="8" r="6"/><path d="M12 14v8"/><path d="M9 19h6"/></svg>
            <div class="ac">Innovia Verified</div>
            <div class="fn">Member in good standing of the Innovia co-op since 2018</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ COMMUNITIES ============ -->
  <section class="v-comm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="head">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow on-accent"><span class="rule-mini"></span>Communities</div>
          <h2>A few of the places we call clients.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>From historic Arcadia enclaves to master-planned communities on the Valley's edge — single-family, condo, and mixed-use, managed end to end.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="cell"><div class="nm">Arcadia Vista</div><div class="meta">Phoenix · 84 doors · since 2011</div><div class="type">Historic single-family HOA</div></div>
        <div class="cell"><div class="nm">Camelback Heights</div><div class="meta">Phoenix · 220 doors · since 2014</div><div class="type">Condominium association</div></div>
        <div class="cell"><div class="nm">Verde Crossing</div><div class="meta">Tempe · 410 doors · since 2016</div><div class="type">Master-planned community</div></div>
        <div class="cell"><div class="nm">Saguaro Bluffs</div><div class="meta">Scottsdale · 156 doors · since 2017</div><div class="type">Townhome / PUD</div></div>
        <div class="cell"><div class="nm">North Reserve</div><div class="meta">N. Scottsdale · 1,040 doors · since 2019</div><div class="type">Master-planned community</div></div>
        <div class="cell"><div class="nm">Mill District Lofts</div><div class="meta">Tempe · 188 doors · since 2021</div><div class="type">Mixed-use condominium</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
